<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43607" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐδείελος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>clear, distinct</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> (only in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i>), usu. of Ithaca, <i><span class="en">
				2.167
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				9.21
			</span></i>, etc.: generally, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦ πού τις νήσων εὐδείελος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					13.234
				</span></i>
			; <i>farseen</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κρόνιον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					1.111
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄστυ</span> Orac. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Eus.
				<u>PE</u>
				6.7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>open to the sun, sunny</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χθὼν Ἰαολκοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					4.76
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κρίση</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Ap.</u>
					438
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅσσα φύει εὐ. αἶα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Euph.
					50
				</span></i>
			. (In signf. <i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i> perh. fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέελος</span> (dub. l.),
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῆλος </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δεᾰλος</span>?): the alternative expl. from
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δείλη</span> (cf. supr. <i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>) given by ancient Gramm., e.g. <i><span class="en">
				Apollon.
				<u>Lex.</u>
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				9.2.41
			</span></i>, does not suit signf. <i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>, but suits the forms.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
